#########
# This file contains diffs between the ABNF version of the grammar
# and a new version which attempts to formalize the elidable
# terminators.
#
# Please do not expect to be able to use thes diffs as a patch; they
# were constructed in very odd ways.
#########


####
# TUhU
#
# tu'u is only 'elidable' at the end of text, since it can include
# essentially *anything*.  So we merely make it optional: if you
# forget to put tu'u in, the tu'e block will just keep eating text
# forever.
####

28a29,30
> ;
> ; A pre-processor should remove everything after the first fa'o.
30,31c32
< text<0> = [1*NAI] [1*CMENE *free / (indicators / 1*free / indicators 1*free)] [joik-jek] text-1
---
> text<0> = [1*NAI] [1*CMENE *free / (indicators / 1*free / indicators 1*free)] [joik-jek] text-1 [FAhO]
45c46
< statement-3<14> = sentence / [tag] TUhE *free text-1 {TUhU *free}
---
> statement-3<14> = sentence / [tag] TUhE *free text-1 [TUhU *free]
217,218d217
< ;
< ; FAhO is a universal terminator and signals the end of parsable input.

####
# VAU
#
# As far as I can tell, everywhere that vau can be used, eliding it
# results in a valid parse.  More importantly, it is not possible to
# determine that the speaker did *not* mean to elide any given vau
# without making a guess as to what you think they actually meant in
# the context of the conversation.  This is not something we can
# expect any computer to do, let alone a CFG.
#
# Example: User means "le nu mi klama vau xamgu".  User says "le nu
# mi klama xamgu".  There is no way to fix that without guessing
# what the user meant to say, because what the user actually said is
# perfectly valid.
#
# Therefore, VAU is made simply optional.
####
52c52
< fragment<20> = ek *free / gihek *free / quantifier / NA *free / terms [VAU *free] / prenex / relative-clauses / links / linkargs
---
> fragment<20> = ek *free / gihek *free / quantifier / NA *free / terms {VAU *free} / prenex / relative-clauses / links / linkargs
70c70
< tail-terms<71> = [terms] [VAU *free]
---
> tail-terms<71> = [terms] {VAU *free}


